course: dictionary
lesson: 10436
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning the writer wants. The word trough is a good example. «A manger, an animal feeding trough» tells you what the word means here: a long box that holds food for animals.
explain: Look at the words around the word. In a science lesson about waves, the words will be about the top and bottom of a wave, so trough means the low point between two waves. On a weather map, trough means a long area of low air pressure that often brings rain.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Trough is a noun: a trough, troughs.
fact: A trough is a long, narrow, open box that holds water or food for animals like pigs, cows or horses.
fact: In science, a trough is the low point between two waves, and the crest is the top.
fact: «Peaks and troughs» means times that are good, followed by times that are bad or low.
fact: Informal: to have your snout in the trough means to take more money or benefits than you should.
exercise: «Jesus was laid in a manger, which is an animal feeding trough.» What is a trough here? | *A long open box that holds food for animals | A long area of low air pressure | A bad time after a good one | A low point between two waves
exercise: In a science lesson about waves, what is the trough? | The middle of a wave | *The low point between two waves | The sound the wave makes | The top of the wave
exercise: «The farm had peaks and troughs that year.» What does troughs mean here? | Long, narrow boxes for food | *Low or bad times after good ones | Times of great happiness | Tall hills
test: On a line graph, what is a trough? | The highest point on the graph | The middle line of the graph | *A low dip in the line | A sharp corner
test: In weather, what does trough mean? | *A long area of low air pressure that often brings rain | A very strong wind | A range of mountains | A sunny, calm day
exam: Ben says, «Mark has his snout in the trough.» What does Ben mean? | *Mark is taking more money or benefits than he should | Mark is swimming in the water trough | Mark is painting the farm fence | Mark is hungry and wants his dinner
